+<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only -->
+
+# Codec 2 (vendored, 3200 bit/s only)
+
+The voice codec of M17 (`CONFIG_M17`, core/m17). A copy of the files of upstream Codec 2 that the 3200 bit/s mode
+needs, nothing else. LGPL-2.1: the license is `COPYING`, each file keeps its own notice. This directory is built only
+with `CONFIG_M17=y`, with the third-party flags (no warnings checked), and can be dropped as a unit.
+
+| Item | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Upstream | https://github.com/drowe67/codec2 |
+| Commit | 310777b1c6f1af0bc7c72f5b32f80f6fd9136962 (2026-03-17), version 1.2.0 |
+| Files | copied unchanged from `src/`, line endings LF |
+| `codebookd.c` | generated: `generate_codebook lsp_cbd src/codebook/dlsp1.txt ... dlsp10.txt` (the input paths in its comments shortened) |
+| `version.h` | `cmake/version.h.in` with the version filled in; reached as `<codec2/version.h>` through `-Icore` |
+
+Build flags (Makefile, tests/host/Makefile): `-DCODEC2_MODE_EN_DEFAULT=0 -DCODEC2_MODE_3200_EN=1` (only the 3200
+mode), `-D__EMBEDDED__ -DNDEBUG`, and `-Dmalloc=codec2_malloc -Dcalloc=codec2_calloc -Dfree=codec2_free`, so every
+allocation (codec2.c, nlp.c, kiss_fft.c) goes to the arena of core/m17/m17_voice.c. All of them happen in
+`codec2_create`; at 512 points the FFTs need no temporary buffers. The other modes' code is referenced from
+`codec2.c` and `quantise.c` but never called: the link needs `--gc-sections` with `-ffunction-sections` (the
+firmware's flags; the host test builds this directory with them too).
+
+Not checked: real-time on a core without an FPU. Codec 2 is floating point; see docs/spec/m17.md.
